<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Almería</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Almeria</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Almería is a port city in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and capital of the province of the same name. It grew into a great port and naval base under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, which built its Alcazaba in the 10th century, and later became the capital of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> kingdom. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> held it briefly in 1147–1157, and the Catholic Monarchs took it in 1489.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/almeria.jpg" alt="Almería" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jebulon · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alcazaba_1,_Almeria,_Spain.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
